# What the integration harness beside this file needs from the machine, declared here because this
# is the only part of the spoon that knows these tools exist. Format is name | kind | locator |
# policy | reason. See Dependencies.spoon for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# Every one is optional, and that is the honest policy rather than a soft one. Nothing in the
# running configuration touches any of this. The harness loads only when a marker file is present,
# which only the suite writes, so a machine missing all of these runs the tool perfectly and simply
# cannot run its tests. Marking them required would claim a breakage that cannot happen.
#
# They are declared all the same, for the reason the setup scripts declare stow and duti. A tool
# that only tooling uses is otherwise the one category nothing checks, and it stops being installed
# without anybody noticing until the day somebody needs it.
jq        | path   | jq                | optional | reads every answer the harness gets back from the browsers and from the agent
osascript | system | /usr/bin/osascript | optional | runs the browser adapters and the accessibility witness that judges each round
open      | system | /usr/bin/open      | optional | carries each command to the harness agent as a URL, since the Hammerspoon CLI blocks while the tool has work in flight
ioreg     | system | /usr/sbin/ioreg    | optional | asks the window server whether the screen is locked, which the accessibility layer cannot be trusted to report about itself
caffeinate | system | /usr/bin/caffeinate | optional | holds the display awake for a run, since a suite drives the machine with synthesised events and the idle timer does not count those
